WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
The departure always comes unexpectedly

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
It is destined to happen like a coincidence

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Your evolving fate starts to grind

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Confused by sudden rain

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Stunned by getting rejected and soaked in the rain

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Let’s laugh it off: a new path will open for you

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
What’s the most precious thing

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
That’s hidden behind meaningless things

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
You can make miracles happen, so keep smiling

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Let’s go wild as you desire

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Have a blast and live it up: that’s my style

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Your Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
| will leave it alone for now

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
So let’s begin our adventure right here

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.658
In the forest of sky burials, a girl was born
to a man’s wife who was supposedly dead.

00:01:37.169 --> 00:01:43.438
Ever since then, guests who stay at Jenhoup’s inn
have often been killed in a mysterious way.

00:01:44.476 --> 00:01:47.639
The villagers gossip that those murdered people

00:01:48.113 --> 00:01:51.810
were offered up
as living sacrifices to revive Larawel...

00:01:52.918 --> 00:01:56.513
and that Jenhoup has sold his soul to the devil.

00:01:57.255 --> 00:01:57.989
And the next victim will be...

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.992
Thé Sun tn Your Patoms
(Setond Part)
And the next victim will be...

00:01:59.992 --> 00:02:01.983
The Sun tn Your Palms
(Setond Part)

00:02:02.361 --> 00:02:04.396
Isn’t that just ridiculous?

00:02:04.396 --> 00:02:06.023
Black magic is make-believe.

00:02:06.264 --> 00:02:07.959
Everyone must be living in a fantasy world.

00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:10.793
A sorceress who contradicts herself, huh?

00:02:11.003 --> 00:02:13.130
Despite the fact that she’s a child
of the fantasy world.

00:02:13.639 --> 00:02:16.631
| don’t really care about black magic or whatever,

00:02:16.942 --> 00:02:20.878
but if he was going to revive someone
with sacrifices, wouldn't it be his murdered wife?

00:02:21.079 --> 00:02:23.047
Why did he pass her over?

00:02:23.315 --> 00:02:24.145
Who knows?

00:02:24.449 --> 00:02:27.552
Maybe it was more convenient
for him if she stayed dead.

00:02:27.552 --> 00:02:29.747
Huh? What do you mean?

00:02:30.555 --> 00:02:34.559
If all those guests who stayed here
were really killed,

00:02:34.559 --> 00:02:37.050
then it’d be a murder case
that should be handled by the police.

00:02:37.396 --> 00:02:39.990
There’s no need for you to act
like a private detective.

00:02:40.699 --> 00:02:45.261
Stop empathizing with every single
person you meet.

00:02:46.038 --> 00:02:47.596
You don’t have to put it like that.

00:02:51.143 --> 00:02:52.508
Hey, Rahzel-chan.

00:02:53.311 --> 00:02:54.278
What?

00:02:55.714 --> 00:02:57.045
Never mind.

00:02:57.282 --> 00:02:59.648
C’mon, let’s go get some breakfast!

00:03:12.064 --> 00:03:16.296
| guess it’s extremely difficult
to find a decent meal in this village.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:17.835
Apparently.

00:03:18.303 --> 00:03:19.998
This isn’t coffee, is it?

00:03:20.238 --> 00:03:22.138
It’s gotta be dirty black water.

00:03:22.507 --> 00:03:27.007
What’s keeping the tourists away is probably
this lousy food, not the murder cases.

00:03:29.214 --> 00:03:33.173
What they need is a decent chef, not the police.

00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:37.746
Larawel and Jenhoup were already gone
when | woke up this morning.

00:03:38.056 --> 00:03:40.684
If | had known this was all we would get,

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:44.053
| would’ve borrowed their kitchen
to make some breakfast myself.

00:03:44.996 --> 00:03:48.830
But | guess | couldn’t have done it
without the innkeeper’s permission.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.096
Whoa, this tastes very unique.

00:03:52.604 --> 00:03:55.732
That’s so careless of them
to both be away from the inn,

00:03:56.274 --> 00:03:59.072
even though we're the only guests.

00:03:59.344 --> 00:04:00.402
Yeah.

00:04:24.236 --> 00:04:25.337
What’s wrong with you?!

00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:26.634
You're insane!

00:04:26.872 --> 00:04:27.861
Why are you doing this?!

00:04:36.915 --> 00:04:39.713
Man, this tea tastes unearthly bland.

00:04:40.018 --> 00:04:43.215
Everything tastes so terrible
that it’s almost hilarious.

00:04:43.555 --> 00:04:44.355
Hey.

00:04:44.356 --> 00:04:45.516
Yeah?

00:04:46.024 --> 00:04:48.322
You were listening in on our
conversation last night, weren’t you?

00:04:50.829 --> 00:04:53.821
Oh, that? | didn’t mean to...

00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:56.190
And what do you have to say?

00:04:56.835 --> 00:04:57.893
I’m sorry.

00:04:58.036 --> 00:04:59.128
That’s all?

00:05:07.179 --> 00:05:10.205
I-l’ll punish myself!

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:20.414
Very well. Your apology is accepted.

00:05:20.892 --> 00:05:21.824
Just kidding.

00:05:22.127 --> 00:05:23.856
| was never mad at you.

00:05:24.162 --> 00:05:26.027
That was just a story from my past.

00:05:26.731 --> 00:05:28.028
Rahzel-chan...

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.361
Okay, that’s enough gloomy stuff!

00:05:30.535 --> 00:05:33.265
Let’s have fun playing a game or two
before Alzeid regains consciousness.

00:05:33.939 --> 00:05:34.406
Specially made by Rahzel’s dad:
Family Name Cards!

00:05:36.441 --> 00:05:38.136
Family Name Cards?

00:05:38.944 --> 00:05:41.003
Wait, what the hell is that, Rahzel-san?

00:05:41.146 --> 00:05:42.704
Like | said, these are playing cards.

00:05:42.948 --> 00:05:44.882
Here’s the instruction manual.

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:49.080
So, instead of numbers,
various family names are written on the cards.

00:05:49.321 --> 00:05:53.121
Instead of suits like hearts or spades,
they are distinguished by characters.

00:05:53.325 --> 00:05:55.054
What? Sounds complicated.

00:05:55.227 --> 00:05:56.361
How creative!

00:05:56.361 --> 00:05:58.625
It’s too creative for me to digest.

00:05:58.897 --> 00:06:02.128
Anyway, how about
we try playing poker with these?

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:06.469
We'll practice without competing first,
so let’s lay the cards on the table.

00:06:08.907 --> 00:06:12.172
Uh, it’s already over my head.

00:06:12.477 --> 00:06:15.969
Suzuki, Suzuki, Sato, Yoshioka, Sakai.

00:06:16.314 --> 00:06:19.147
You rock, Heat-tan! You already got one pair.

00:06:19.451 --> 00:06:20.247
| rock?!

00:06:20.352 --> 00:06:21.250
Let’s see mine...

00:06:21.786 --> 00:06:25.051
Miyamoto, Sato, Suzuki, Suzuki, and Suzuki.

00:06:25.457 --> 00:06:27.425
Is it just me or are there too many Suzukis?

00:06:27.425 --> 00:06:29.586
Clearly there are.

00:06:30.095 --> 00:06:32.689
The rules are the same as poker, right?

00:06:33.465 --> 00:06:35.933
All right, I'll change three cards.

00:06:36.368 --> 00:06:38.598
One... Two... Huh?!

00:06:39.104 --> 00:06:40.905
How come only this guy has a full name?

00:06:48.914 --> 00:06:50.882
How could a joker be a trick?

00:06:50.882 --> 00:06:52.782
And that’s gotta be Linda.

00:06:52.884 --> 00:06:56.285
Linda is a mysterious woman.
She might be under a false name.

00:06:56.454 --> 00:06:58.513
What’s up with that overly complicated setting?

00:06:58.823 --> 00:07:00.484
ll change my cards, too.

00:07:01.192 --> 00:07:02.318
Let’s see...

00:07:03.028 --> 00:07:06.725
Wow, a full house
with three Suzukis and two Satos.

00:07:07.098 --> 00:07:08.429
What’s the point of this?

00:07:08.867 --> 00:07:11.802
| have one Michael, and the rest are all Suzukis.

00:07:12.237 --> 00:07:13.972
Just how many Suzukis are there?

00:07:13.972 --> 00:07:16.463
Wow, that’s awesome, Heat-tan!
You have four of a kind!

00:07:16.741 --> 00:07:19.073
Wait, it’s actually five of a kind
including the Michael.

00:07:19.444 --> 00:07:22.313
Okay, now that we both know the rules,
let’s play for real.

00:07:22.314 --> 00:07:23.474
Time to deal!

00:07:31.323 --> 00:07:32.620
Alzeid?

00:07:33.425 --> 00:07:35.260
A Nagashima four of a kind!

00:07:36.895 --> 00:07:38.123
A Nagashima...

00:07:38.496 --> 00:07:40.191
...four of a kind?!

00:07:40.565 --> 00:07:43.830
| just got a Michael,
so | thought | could win!

00:07:44.135 --> 00:07:47.127
| used to be called the King of Cards.

00:07:47.439 --> 00:07:51.102
How could you be good at this
so fast? You traitor!

00:07:52.344 --> 00:07:53.812
And this Michael here, too!

00:07:57.916 --> 00:07:58.245
I’m more concerned about what’s gonna happen
to him, rather than the game itself.

00:07:58.917 --> 00:08:01.112
Jeez... Something’s wrong with you guys!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.645
Snap out of it! Don't get too into this!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.229
Wasn't that...

00:08:23.775 --> 00:08:24.673
What’s wrong?

00:08:24.909 --> 00:08:26.774
Um, it’s just...

00:08:26.978 --> 00:08:28.379
Let’s go back now.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:29.210
Sure.

00:08:48.233 --> 00:08:49.131
Larawel?

00:08:49.601 --> 00:08:50.693
Rahzel-san.

00:08:54.639 --> 00:08:57.335
What’s going on?
Are they coming towards this inn?

00:08:59.511 --> 00:09:01.604
A crowd of villagers are heading this way.

00:09:01.946 --> 00:09:03.641
Let’s get out of here quickly.

00:09:04.182 --> 00:09:05.740
| have a feeling we’d better stay out of this.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:08.714
Yeah. Come with us, Larawel.

00:09:08.953 --> 00:09:11.251
Um, but Daddy is still...

00:09:12.357 --> 00:09:15.952
Oh, right. What’s Jenhoup up to
now of all times?

00:09:16.294 --> 00:09:20.253
I’m not sure. Ever since he returned home,
he’s locked himself in that room.

00:09:20.565 --> 00:09:21.554
That room’?

00:09:36.314 --> 00:09:37.975
Come out, Jenhoup!

00:09:38.316 --> 00:09:40.079
What the hell did you do to my son?!

00:09:40.718 --> 00:09:44.521
There’s a witness who saw you
wandering around the area!

00:09:44.522 --> 00:09:48.390
We tolerated your misdeeds toward
your own guests, but this is unforgivable!

00:09:48.993 --> 00:09:50.961
Come outside, you murderer!

00:09:56.835 --> 00:09:57.631
Watch out!

00:09:59.104 --> 00:10:00.002
This isn’t good.

00:10:00.238 --> 00:10:02.968
| don’t think they’re up
for a peaceful discussion.

00:10:05.176 --> 00:10:06.165
Larawell!

00:10:09.447 --> 00:10:10.607
Please stop!

00:10:12.016 --> 00:10:14.416
Daddy is not a murderer!

00:10:14.819 --> 00:10:16.980
Then, who did it?

00:10:17.155 --> 00:10:18.189
Don’t interfere!

00:10:18.189 --> 00:10:20.054
If you’re gonna defend him,
you're equally guilty!

00:10:20.225 --> 00:10:24.389
That’s right. Everything started to go wrong
ever since you showed up here.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:27.691
You goddamn monster!

00:10:32.237 --> 00:10:33.363
Rahzel-san.

00:10:33.972 --> 00:10:37.066
Stop acting so childish towards such a little girl.

00:10:37.375 --> 00:10:41.545
As | see it, your behavior is far more monstrous.

00:10:41.546 --> 00:10:43.411
What? You're their accomplice?

00:10:43.715 --> 00:10:46.582
Just hear me out, you Baldy!

00:10:48.553 --> 00:10:50.748
Wow, impressive overthrow.

00:10:51.523 --> 00:10:53.354
What the hell is with you guys?

00:10:53.758 --> 00:10:55.919
You outsiders shouldn't talk
like you know everything.

00:10:56.427 --> 00:10:59.029
Jenhoup, are you gonna keep hiding like that?

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.863
If you wanna play rough,
we're just gonna smoke you out!

00:11:03.701 --> 00:11:05.293
Hey! What’s the idea?!

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:07.196
Please, stop it.

00:11:12.043 --> 00:11:15.103
I’m the one to blame for everything.

00:11:18.716 --> 00:11:19.648
Daddy...

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:27.490
As you all suspect,
Larawel isn’t my real child.

00:11:29.527 --> 00:11:32.963
| know that everyone talks
about me behind my back.

00:11:33.264 --> 00:11:37.724
You're right. There’s no way my dead wife
could’ve given birth to a child.

00:11:38.069 --> 00:11:42.028
Larawel was an abandoned child that | found
at the graveyard where my wife’s buried...

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:46.974
and I’m the one who killed my wife.

00:11:54.085 --> 00:11:55.245
Listen...

00:11:56.487 --> 00:11:58.921
Will you divorce me?

00:12:00.758 --> 00:12:02.316
Is this some kind of joke?

00:12:02.627 --> 00:12:04.959
We're having a child soon.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.359
It’s not your child.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.360
I’ve been seeing someone else.

00:12:11.402 --> 00:12:14.667
He says we can live together,
along with this child.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.937
| want to leave you and find my happiness.

00:12:30.021 --> 00:12:32.012
| didn’t regret it.

00:12:32.557 --> 00:12:35.651
Although, | thought the life
that was about to be born was innocent,

00:12:36.027 --> 00:12:38.086
even if it wasn’t my biological child.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:04.211
Somehow, it felt to me as though that child
had been carried by my wife.

00:13:11.462 --> 00:13:12.827
What the hell is this room?

00:13:13.264 --> 00:13:14.959
So, it’s true about the black magic...

00:13:25.743 --> 00:13:32.615
Loving and protecting Larawel was how
| made atonement for my wife and the child...

00:13:32.917 --> 00:13:37.183
so, | couldn’t forgive anyone
who tried to hurt her.

00:13:37.555 --> 00:13:41.025
| intended to take the life of those
who threw rocks at her

00:13:41.025 --> 00:13:45.462
or called her names, using this room.

00:13:45.697 --> 00:13:47.688
So you killed my son here...

00:13:51.135 --> 00:13:55.697
But in the end, | was the one
who caused her the deepest pain.

00:13:59.243 --> 00:14:01.040
It’s over, Larawel.

00:14:01.245 --> 00:14:05.079
I’m sorry, there’s no other way
for me to help you.

00:14:20.398 --> 00:14:22.696
Th-this isn’t acceptable.

00:14:23.167 --> 00:14:26.625
There’s no way | could accept this!

00:14:36.647 --> 00:14:37.705
Rahzel-chan?

00:14:40.184 --> 00:14:42.948
Are you still bothered
that we left Larawel behind?

00:14:44.689 --> 00:14:49.183
What if that altar
was all staged only for yesterday?

00:14:49.994 --> 00:14:56.695
You mean, he took advantage of the villagers’
belief in satanic rituals and black magic?

00:14:57.235 --> 00:14:59.897
In order to distract their attention
from the real killer,

00:15:00.338 --> 00:15:02.533
he performed this outrageous
stunt to mislead them.

00:15:03.174 --> 00:15:05.870
Then he drew their attention
with the shocking confession,

00:15:06.344 --> 00:15:08.471
and ended it with his own death.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.244
In other words, there’s a real
killer somewhere out there?

00:15:14.719 --> 00:15:17.517
The only person Jenhoup
would go that far to protect is...

00:15:19.123 --> 00:15:20.715
I don’t want to believe it.

00:15:21.426 --> 00:15:23.587
| wish | could prove that I’m wrong.

00:15:24.796 --> 00:15:27.230
Mind if we go back?

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.409
A guest at this hour?

00:15:41.145 --> 00:15:42.407
Who is it?

00:15:55.226 --> 00:15:56.250
Larawel?

00:15:57.528 --> 00:16:00.053
That’s odd. The door isn’t locked.

00:16:14.378 --> 00:16:15.402
Larawel...

00:16:16.047 --> 00:16:18.038
Please, don’t give me that look.

00:16:18.583 --> 00:16:20.107
| was only defending myself.

00:16:20.518 --> 00:16:25.285
He tried to kill me to take revenge
for his son’s death.

00:16:27.158 --> 00:16:31.060
Will you answer the question
that | asked you last night?

00:16:31.629 --> 00:16:36.566
"?'m a murderer. Don’t you find me freaky?"

00:16:36.968 --> 00:16:40.267
| don’t find you freaky,
but | don’t understand you.

00:16:40.938 --> 00:16:42.303
| don’t get it, Larawel!

00:16:44.509 --> 00:16:49.674
| was four years old
when | first killed someone.

00:16:50.882 --> 00:16:55.080
A guest’s lighted cigarette burned me
as we passed each other.

00:17:01.459 --> 00:17:02.426
It hurt.

00:17:03.528 --> 00:17:05.257
That was all that happened.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:06.924
Just for that.

00:17:08.099 --> 00:17:09.498
Isn't it ridiculous?

00:17:09.901 --> 00:17:13.860
For something that trivial,
I’ve already killed seven people.

00:17:15.406 --> 00:17:18.170
Daddy always took care of the bodies.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:20.577
He was such a sweet man.

00:17:21.145 --> 00:17:24.376
He was willing to make
any sacrifices to protect me.

00:17:24.615 --> 00:17:25.877
| loved him so much.

00:17:27.585 --> 00:17:34.286
Every time, | told myself that | must stop doing this
and causing Daddy any more trouble.

00:17:34.792 --> 00:17:36.282
But | couldn't stop myself.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:40.419
| don’t even know why | keep doing this.

00:17:40.831 --> 00:17:44.528
| don't even want to kill anyone;
| don't even hate anyone.

00:17:45.536 --> 00:17:46.370
Larawel.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.098
Stay back!

00:17:48.539 --> 00:17:49.506
Rahzel-chan!

00:18:03.521 --> 00:18:04.385
Larawell!

00:18:04.722 --> 00:18:06.490
Let me ask you one more time:

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:10.620
"?'m a murderer. Don’t you find me freaky?"

00:18:11.228 --> 00:18:14.356
You’re a murderer just like | am.
| want you to tell me.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:28.142
Suffering from a fatal illness,
my mother started losing her mind.

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:35.119
My father couldn’t stand it and left the family,
which drove her even more insane.

00:18:36.087 --> 00:18:39.579
Having incurable anxiety,
she gradually started taking it out on me.

00:18:40.224 --> 00:18:45.787
And one day, when | felt my life was in danger...

00:18:48.499 --> 00:18:53.402
When my father finally returned,
he took me deep into the forest.

00:18:54.338 --> 00:18:55.327
Rahzel-chan?

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:01.002
However | answer, | doubt it will satisfy you.

00:19:05.416 --> 00:19:08.749
But | still don’t want to let go of your hand.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:14.924
Since you never hesitate to reach out
your hand, | get the wrong idea...

00:19:15.826 --> 00:19:22.459
that someone like me might be forgiven
and someday lead a normal life.

00:19:26.103 --> 00:19:29.038
That’s not possible. How stupid am |?

00:19:29.507 --> 00:19:30.531
Larawell!

00:19:31.375 --> 00:19:33.536
Do you remember the assignment?

00:19:33.944 --> 00:19:35.036
Assignment?

00:19:35.946 --> 00:19:40.747
So, Larawel. Are you scared of me?
Do you find me freaky?

00:19:41.218 --> 00:19:42.242
No.

00:19:42.653 --> 00:19:43.244
How come?

00:19:43.888 --> 00:19:45.150
I’m not sure.

00:19:45.456 --> 00:19:47.321
Then, this is your next assignment.

00:19:47.858 --> 00:19:52.158
Think as hard as you can,
and let’s check your answer tomorrow.

00:19:53.164 --> 00:19:54.893
| have my answer now.

00:19:56.901 --> 00:19:59.597
lt was because the hand
you reached out was so warm.

00:20:00.438 --> 00:20:03.168
So warm like the sun...

00:20:06.977 --> 00:20:08.774
Damn, let’s get out of here!

00:20:14.652 --> 00:20:15.414
Why?

00:20:16.387 --> 00:20:20.619
Why can’t my hand reach anything
when it needs to?

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:30.189
| couldn’t reach her helpless hand,
and couldn’t save her helpless eyes.

00:20:38.843 --> 00:20:41.345
What’s she doing?

00:20:41.345 --> 00:20:42.412
Dunno.

00:20:42.413 --> 00:20:46.913
Apparently, Larawel wanted to fly in the sky,
so she’s probably trying to give her a sense of it.

00:20:49.186 --> 00:20:53.179
| suppose she somehow
projects her own past on to Larawel.

00:20:53.457 --> 00:20:57.621
You eavesdropped on her past,
and now, you're sharing it with me?

00:20:57.928 --> 00:20:59.293
You're disgusting.

00:20:59.563 --> 00:21:00.791
Like | care.

00:21:01.031 --> 00:21:03.066
But now you're equally to blame.

00:21:03.067 --> 00:21:05.194
You better punish yourself, too, Al-kiddo.

00:21:05.603 --> 00:21:06.695
Don’t be silly.

00:21:07.004 --> 00:21:09.700
You just committed another crime, that’s all.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.432
Huh? Is that right?

00:21:15.679 --> 00:21:17.647
What are you moping around for, Idiot?

00:21:17.948 --> 00:21:18.539
Let’s go.

00:21:19.083 --> 00:21:20.914
Okay, okay, I’m coming—

00:21:21.952 --> 00:21:22.816
Here.

00:21:28.292 --> 00:21:28.883
Sure.

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
As | hear the sound of laughter

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Coming from the room next door

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
| slowly wake up to the morning that | adore

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Somewhere | dreamed of a painting

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
| just painted a new chair for you

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Even if the sorrowful story

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Is lying in wait beyond the curtain

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Even if we may feel like strangers tomorrow

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
| believe in the perfect miracle that you'll still be here

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
The hand you reached out shows no sign of parting

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
As | grow teary-eyed, | just want to hold you now
